yunmai-noble-desktop
====================

The dashboard and the simulator control app are a single package with no
service of its own. Start it from the application menu, or directly:

  yunmai-noble-desktop
  yunmai-noble-desktop --historian http://pi.local:3000

YUNMAI_HISTORIAN_URL overrides the default http://127.0.0.1:3000 for the
menu entry. The client probes /health before opening; when the URL is
loopback and the service is not running, it starts yunmai-noble.service
and waits for it. Set YUNMAI_AUTOSTART=none (or pass --no-autostart) to
disable that.

Settings in the titlebar selects the active driver (simulator, D-Bus, or
node bindings) and remembers the choice in
~/.config/yunmai-noble/desktop.json. When the simulator driver is active,
"Open simulator" launches yunmai-noble-simulator-ui, which drives
/api/suite/simulator and never touches D-Bus.

Install yunmai-noble for the local service, or yunmai-noble-full for the
service and this client together.
